import graphics.dl

to get a native UI [font] in {a pointer to UI view:view} from {C string:path} sized {integer:size}:
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    set loading to the result of loading a font from path at size size rasterized at scale 2 for (surface's resource)
    require condition (loading succeeded) reporting "Loading a UI font failed"
    set face to @intrinsic("construct", native UI face, loading's typeface, size)
    return (storage for one slot initialized with face) as a pointer

to release native UI font {a pointer:resource}:
    set face to resource as a pointer to native UI face
    set result to the result of releasing (the address of (face's typeface))
    require condition (result succeeded) reporting "Releasing a UI font failed"
    deallocate face

to get the native UI width of {a pointer:resource} containing {C string:text} counting {integer:count}:
    set face to resource as a pointer to native UI face
    return the width of (a new string from text containing count bytes) using (face's typeface)

to draw native UI text in {a pointer to UI view:view} using {a pointer:resource} containing {C string:text} counting {integer:count} at {floating-point number:x} {floating-point number:y} in {a pointer to UI paint:ink}:
    set face to resource as a pointer to native UI face
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    set state to surface's resource as a pointer to DynlexGraphics
    set native UI clipping in view
    set zero to UI surface point (UI point (a UI point at 0.0 and 0.0) transformed by (view's transform)) in view
    set east to UI surface point (UI point (a UI point at 1.0 and 0.0) transformed by (view's transform)) in view
    set south to UI surface point (UI point (a UI point at 0.0 and 1.0) transformed by (view's transform)) in view
    set model to an identity graphics matrix
    store ((east's x - zero's x) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into model at 0
    store ((east's y - zero's y) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into model at 1
    store ((south's x - zero's x) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into model at 4
    store ((south's y - zero's y) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into model at 5
    store (zero's x as a 32 bit floating-point number) into model at 12
    store (zero's y as a 32 bit floating-point number) into model at 13
    set state's model to model
    set result to the result of drawing (a new string from text containing count bytes) as text at x x and y y using (face's typeface) in color red (ink's red), green (ink's green) and blue (ink's blue) in (surface's frame)
    require condition (result succeeded) reporting "Drawing UI text failed"
    set state's model to an identity graphics matrix
